// ERROR: no field or method named `drain`
// ADR-0089 §AMEND Slice 2b — T2b-standalone-refuse (điều kiện thép G #1):
// `drain` is a FOR-GUARD-ONLY pseudo-method (§2b.2) — it is not registered
// in `builtin_method_type`/trait dispatch, so a standalone `v.drain()`
// (outside a `for` iterable position) falls through the ordinary
// MethodCall path to `TypeError::UnknownMember` (E1015 — the SAME code any
// other unrecognized method name would hit; its `Display` text embeds no
// literal "E1015" string, so this fixture matches the message text
// instead, same convention as fixtures 51/52/55/56/57/470). MEASURED, not
// guessed: the ADR text describes this generically as a "method not
// found"/E1041 refuse, but E1041 `NoMatchingOverload` is reserved for
// Call-style overloaded builtins (`push`/`pop_front`/`len`/`get`) resolved
// through `resolve_overload` — a path a MethodCall receiver never reaches.
// This discrepancy is flagged to O/G in the WO report (D, ADR-0089 Slice
// 2b) — the fixture asserts the CODE'S ACTUAL behavior, not the ADR prose.
function main() -> Integer {
    let mutable xs = vector_new();
    xs = push(xs, 1);
    let x = xs.drain();
    return 0;
}
